  "title": "Two ways to reduce covered call asymmetry: strike out or in the money",
  "summary": "Covered calls have negative asymmetry: capped upside, open downside. Strike the calls out of the money to keep more upside if you are bullish. Strike them in the money to get intrinsic value that cushions a fall if you are bearish. At the money fits a flat view. There is no right answer, but you need a view on the stock.",
